{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"CLSA-2026-1795615684","published":"2026-11-25T14:08:16Z","modified":"2026-11-26T07:45:05.970252402Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-78659","CVE-2026-97033","CVE-2026-97036","CVE-2026-97037","CVE-2026-97042"],"summary":"golang: Fix of 5 CVEs","details":"- CVE-2026-78659: net/http - charge every field name declared in an HTTP/2\n  \"Trailer\" header against a separate trailer header list budget, so a\n  client can no longer make the server allocate a disproportionate amount\n  of memory for Request.Trailer\n- CVE-2026-97033: cmd/go - disallow --sysroot and -target in cgo flags,\n  reject -isysroot and -Wl,-syslibroot naming a regular file, and restrict\n  -x to the languages cgo supports, preventing code execution at build time\n- CVE-2026-97036: cmd/go - disallow \"-l to_library\" and the -lazy_library,\n  -lazy_framework, -load_hidden, -library and -library-path linker flags in\n  cgo LDFLAGS, and check recombined -l arguments against disallowed flags,\n  preventing an arbitrary LTO plugin or linker script from being loaded\n- CVE-2026-97037: cmd/go - require a -Wl, prefix on the second token of split\n  -Wl, flags and reject linker script files passed through -framework,\n  -Wl,-framework, -Wl,-undefined, -Wl,--just-symbols, -Wl,-R, -Wl,-subsystem\n  and -Wl,-sectcreate, preventing code execution at link time\n- CVE-2026-97042: cmd/cgo, cmd/compile, cmd/link - validate every character\n  of cgo_import_dynamic library names and reject \"..\" path traversal, also\n  in cgo-generated files for Windows, and reject PE imported DLL names with\n  path separators, \"..\", \":\" or a leading \"-\" or \"@\"","affected":[{"package":{"name":"go-toolset","ecosystem":"TuxCare:AlmaLinux:9.2","purl":"pkg:rpm/tuxcare/go-toolset?distro=almalinux-9.2"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"1.22.9-1.el9_2.tuxcare.els33"}]}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://github.com/cloudlinux/tuxcare-osv/tree/main/data/els_os/almalinux9.2es